WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00.330 --> 00:06.560
Well, we are still on our EPIC journey, and we have gone through style and delivery in conversation.

2
00:07.240 --> 00:09.470
But last, but not least, is facilitation.

3
00:10.530 --> 00:12.640
Facilitation is absolutely critical.

4
00:13.160 --> 00:16.510
Facilitation means to make something easier.

5
00:17.060 --> 00:26.154
And that is why effective communicators are also effective facilitators, because they know how to make it easier for other people to understand their message.

6
00:26.154 --> 00:31.680
Oftentimes people think that being a facilitator means you actually have to lead the discussion,

7
00:31.880 --> 00:35.300
or that you need to be the content expert in a conversation.

8
00:35.750 --> 00:38.767
That is not the case. Anyone can be a facilitator.

9
00:38.767 --> 00:50.110
An effective facilitator comes in with a mindset that is open and curious, and really “over there”. We had discussed this in earlier sessions: the “over there” and the “over here” mindset.

10
00:50.890 --> 00:54.340
“Over there” is really with your audience, with other people,

11
00:54.890 --> 00:56.260
thinking about them,

12
00:56.650 --> 01:01.890
thinking about where they may be, being willing to release your agenda when it’s appropriate,

13
01:02.920 --> 01:07.550
thinking about asking questions and really uncovering

14
01:07.940 --> 01:09.600
what else is going on in the room.

15
01:10.050 --> 01:13.920
Facilitation is equally important whether you are interacting with one

16
01:14.850 --> 01:19.650
person or a large group. Some of the techniques that we will look at include

17
01:20.040 --> 01:21.670
the open–narrow–close framework.

18
01:22.440 --> 01:26.500
This is one way of at least structuring a conversation and understanding a

19
01:26.920 --> 01:30.690
kind of overall architecture you can use for most conversations.

20
01:31.140 --> 01:36.320
So there are lots of ways you’ll learn how to use all of the steps from before:

21
01:36.710 --> 01:40.510
bringing in the empathy, understanding the purpose of that meeting,

22
01:41.160 --> 01:47.940
drawing out those insights — whether you’re bringing them to the meeting, and others are also contributing those in the interaction —

23
01:48.390 --> 01:51.750
and bringing that all together in a well-orchestrated conversation.

